535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483514 1079 #uuid "58512abd-62af-54c3-b5c3-67149278f4ae" 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483515 1068 #edb/ref 17592186483518 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483515 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483515 1071 "Calculate $\\int x\\sqrt{x^{2} - 20}\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\nWork on an interval where $x^{2} - 20>0$." 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483515 1072 #uuid "60241274-8490-524b-acba-fc74aea3d5e9" 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483515 1074 "In this case, the $x$ outside the parentheses isn't quite the derivative of $(x^{2} - 20).$ But the derivative is $2 x,$ so we're only out by a constant factor.\n\nSo we make the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x^{2} - 20.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nand we can now write our integral in terms of $u,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int x\\sqrt{x^{2} - 20}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\int u^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve the integral in terms of $u$ and then write the final result in terms of $x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\int u^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\,\\text{d}u &=\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{u^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{\\frac{3}{2}}+C\\\\ &=\\frac{1}{3}u^{\\frac{3}{2}}+C\\\\ &=\\frac{\\left(x^{2} - 20\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483516 1080 "\\frac{\\left(- x^{2} + 11\\right)^{4}}{2}+C" 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483516 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483516 1083 #uuid "62d8dfd9-a6bd-508a-9775-552281a549c3" 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483517 1080 "\\frac{\\left(- x^{2} + 11\\right)^{4}}{4}+C" 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483517 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483517 1083 #uuid "6a43b002-ea