ft(- x^{2} + 11\\right)^{4}}{4}+C" 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483523 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483523 1083 #uuid "d49c5348-be43-503f-8745-e317361c550b" 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483524 1068 #edb/ref 17592186483514 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483524 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483524 1071 "$\\int x\\left(- x^{2} + 11\\right)^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483524 1072 #uuid "f11633ad-c3d3-53f8-93e6-d3a1d7d686df" 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483524 1074 "In this case, the $x$ outside the parentheses isn't quite the derivative of $(- x^{2} + 11).$ But the derivative is $- 2 x,$ so we're only out by a constant factor.\n\nSo we make the substitution\n\n$$\nu=- x^{2} + 11.\n$$\n\nIts derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=- 2 x\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad - \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nand we can now write our integral in terms of $u,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int x\\left(- x^{2} + 11\\right)^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=- \\frac{1}{2}\\int u^{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve the integral in terms of $u$ and then write the final result in terms of $x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{1}{2}\\int u^{3}\\,\\text{d}u &=- \\frac{1}{2}\\frac{u^{4}}{4}+C\\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{8}u^{4}+C\\\\ &=- \\frac{\\left(- x^{2} + 11\\right)^{4}}{8}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483525 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186068723.py" 13194139535231 17592186045443 true] [17592186483525 1169 #uuid "6d27df3f-00b8-523f-a56c-43a057ae4954" 13194139535231 17592186045443 true]] :edb/tempids {"0ef1452f-8922-5c41-aad6-b2506e9df8ed" 17592186483511 "12fef86c-0c97-50c4-9487-6d40fc7b6a2e" 17592186483512 "26ddfda2-b2b6-595c-8b7e-f782a80088e3" 17592186483513 "58512abd-62af-54c3-b5c3-67149278f4ae" 17592186483514 "60241274-8490-524b-acba-fc74aea3